# PRINCESS ELEWYN

A pale face watches you from the tower window. "Another visitor? The birds will be jealous. What would you like to know?"

> 1 The tower
"Two hundred and twelve steps. I have counted them every day since Father sent me here."

"The door is locked from the outside, and the only key hangs from the gaoler's belt."

> 2 The birds
"The thrushes come first, then the finches. They bring me news of the valley, and I read them stories in return."

"They like the ones with dragons best."

> 3 The king
"Father means well. He thinks a tower can keep out every danger in the world."

"It keeps out everything else, too."

> 4 Heroes
"Every knight in my books rides out at dawn and returns a hero. I would settle for riding out at all."

"Are you a hero? You look more like someone who is lost."
